window.docContents[33].resolve({"/Onboarding___-Human-Context-Protocols/L5-___-The-oscillation-dies-out/#A-Property-Kind-Calculus-for-Metrology___-proving-quantity-and-unit-laws-in-Lean___-from-ISO___IEC-80000-to-measurement-uncertainty--Onboarding___-Human-Context-Protocols--L5-___-The-oscillation-dies-out--Synopsis--Verifiable-properties":{"contents":"* The damped oscillator's energy decreases at the rate stated by PhysLib's energy-dissipation theorem (theorem) HCP.L5_Damping#energy_dissipation.* decayRateOf divides A's γ by A's 2m, and its magnitude equals PhysLib's decayRate; using B's mass instead fails with a type mismatch (refused) HCP.L5_Damping#kinds_and_decay_rate.* δ and ω₀ have the same dimension, T⁻¹, and adding them fails to type-check (refused) HCP.L5_Damping#same_dimension_different_kinds.* PhysLib's IsUnderdamped is equivalent to δ < ω₀. Comparing the two as kinded quantities fails with a type mismatch, because their kinds differ; IsUnderdamped implies that the magnitude of δ is less than the magnitude of ω₀ (theorem) HCP.L5_Damping#underdamped_regime.* Subtracting an earlier record of A's δ from a later one type-checks as an IndividualQuantity about A of the damping-coefficient kind, whose magnitude is the difference of the two decay rates; subtracting B's δ from A's fails with a type mismatch (type-checked) HCP.L5_Damping#same_oscillator_states.\n\n","context":"A Property Kind Calculus for Metrology: proving quantity and unit laws in Lean, from ISO/IEC 80000 to measurement uncertainty\u0009Onboarding: Human Context Protocols\u0009L5 — The oscillation dies out\u0009Synopsis","header":"5.6.1.3. Verifiable properties","id":"/Onboarding___-Human-Context-Protocols/L5-___-The-oscillation-dies-out/#A-Property-Kind-Calculus-for-Metrology___-proving-quantity-and-unit-laws-in-Lean___-from-ISO___IEC-80000-to-measurement-uncertainty--Onboarding___-Human-Context-Protocols--L5-___-The-oscillation-dies-out--Synopsis--Verifiable-properties"}});